    {
      "deviation": "GitHub puts Markdown at 261.42, inside a seven-family run -- python 246.50, xml 251.44, typescript 253.30, powershell 258.14, markdown, lua 264.05, php 272.03 -- and it read as Python's blue. Markdown is the most-viewed family in the app and Python's colour is the better known of the two, so Markdown is the one that moves. 276.0 clears every other family by 0.0355 rather than 0.0149 and is still plainly a blue rather than a violet. The rank puts it below the band, which is the deliberate part: at its upstream rank it painted 0.571 against Python's 0.599, and no hue move makes a lighter blue read as a darker one. #083fa1 is a dark navy, so this paints closer to the colour GitHub chose than the band alone allowed.",
